<%# A returned review's checklist: the reviewer's asks, rendered as boxes the
    builder has to tick before the resubmission is accepted. See
    Certification::Reviewable for the "- do the thing" syntax reviewers write.

    Nothing here is persisted. The digest pins the checklist this form was built
    from, so a reviewer who rewords their feedback while the modal sits open is
    caught by ActionItemGate rather than having stale ticks accepted against
    items that no longer exist.

    Only the asks appear here, never the reviewer's surrounding prose - that is
    already on the timeline card behind this modal (projects/_review_feedback),
    so repeating it would bury the checklist in text the builder just read.

    Must be rendered inside a form carrying data-controller="action-items", so
    the submit event this partial's targets guard reaches the controller.

    Locals: review - a returned Certification::Reviewable. %>
<div class="action-items" data-action-items-target="block">
  <%# Copy for both states lives here rather than in the controller, so the
      wording stays with the rest of the view. %>
  <h4 class="action-items__heading"
      data-action-items-target="heading"
      data-pending="Before you submit again"
      data-ready="Ready to submit!">Before you submit again</h4>
  <p class="action-items__hint">Your last reviewer asked for these changes. Tick each one to confirm you've done it.</p>

  <ul class="action-items__list">
    <% review.action_items.each_with_index do |item, index| %>
      <li class="action-items__item">
        <label class="action-items__label">
          <%# id: nil because the name repeats across the list, so Rails would
              otherwise stamp every box with the same element id. The label wraps
              its input, so nothing needs to point at one. %>
          <%= check_box_tag "acknowledged_action_items[]", index, false,
                id: nil,
                class: "action-items__checkbox",
                data: { action_items_target: "checkbox", action: "change->action-items#report" } %>
          <span class="action-items__text"><%= item %></span>
        </label>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>

  <p class="action-items__progress" data-action-items-target="progress" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="action-items__error" role="alert" data-action-items-target="error" hidden></p>

  <%= hidden_field_tag "action_items_digest", review.action_items_digest, id: nil %>
</div>
